\question[8] The following table shows the number of books of $3$ different genres.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|l|c|}
\hline
\textbf{Genres} & \textbf{Number of books} \\
\hline
Science Fiction & $1824$ \\
Mystery         & $?$ \\
Romance         & $?$ \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

\begin{parts}
    \part If there are $8$ libraries in Hong Kong, can all the books be evenly distributed to all the libraries? Explain your answer.

    \begin{solutionorlines}[4cm]
    \end{solutionorlines}

    \part In the libraries, only books of the same genre can be placed on the same bookshelf, and each bookshelf has the same number of books.
